# Goal Description
Adapt the existing [setup.sh](file:///c:/projects/github/casaos-home-server/setup.sh) home server script to support ZimaOS-style deployments. This involves adding branding, menu options, and specific configurations for ZimaOS (which is the evolved version of CasaOS).

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Setup Script

#### [MODIFY] [setup.sh](file:///c:/projects/github/casaos-home-server/setup.sh)
- Update `HEADER_ART` to include ZimaOS branding.
- Add a choice for "ZimaOS-Style Setup" in the main menu.
- Update [install_casaos](file:///c:/projects/github/casaos-home-server/setup.sh#168-405) to use the `v0.5.0-beta` installer for ZimaOS flavor.
- Implement Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble) compatibility fixes (e.g., forcing `OS_RELEASE=jammy` if necessary).
- **[ALTERNATIVE]** Instructions for a clean WSL2 Ubuntu 22.04 installation for maximum stability.
- Provide manual instructions for adding the ZimaOS App Store JSON if automatic registration fails.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `bash -n setup.sh` to check for syntax errors.
- Simulate the script using `--dry-run` to ensure all paths and logic for ZimaOS selection work as intended.

### Manual Verification
- Ask the user to run the script and select the new ZimaOS option.
- Verify that the app stores are correctly registered and the branding is displayed.
